expr main (could care less)

let message "The idiom is `couldn't care less`: you care so little that you could not care any less."
let description "Corrects the common slip `could care less` to the idiom `couldn't care less`."
let kind "Usage"
let becomes "couldn't care less"

test "I could care less." "I couldn't care less."
test "Honestly, I could care less about the game." "Honestly, I couldn't care less about the game."
test "She could care less what they think." "She couldn't care less what they think."
test "They could care less if it rains." "They couldn't care less if it rains."
test "He said he could care less." "He said he couldn't care less."
test "We could care less about the score." "We couldn't care less about the score."
test "I COULD CARE LESS." "I COULDN'T CARE LESS."
test "Frankly I could care less, to be honest." "Frankly I couldn't care less, to be honest."

allows "I couldn't care less."
allows "I could not care less about it."
allows "She couldn't care less what they think."
allows "I could care for the dog while you are away."
allows "You could care more about your health."
allows "They could take less time."
